  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "4334e3e6-1d42-49c3-9f61-2b75293d6495",
    "name": "superForum",
    "description": "# superForum API — end-to-end collection\n\nA runnable, happy-path walkthrough of the superForum REST API: sign in, create a\ncommunity, write a post and a comment, vote, read everything back, then tidy up.\nThe folders are ordered as a full resource lifecycle, so the whole collection runs\ntop to bottom in a single pass.\n\n## Setup\n\n1. Start the API locally — `npm run dev` (serves `http://localhost:3000`).\n2. Create a Postman **environment** with three variables:\n   - `baseUrl`     — `http://localhost:3000/api`\n   - `supabaseUrl` — your Supabase project URL (`https://<project>.supabase.co`)\n   - `supabaseKey` — the Supabase publishable / anon key\n\n   You don't set `token`, `userId`, `communityId`, `postId`, or `commentId` — the\n   requests capture those automatically as they run.\n\n## Running it\n\nRun the folders in order (Collection Runner, or top to bottom by hand) against a\n**fresh database**:\n\n**Auth → Communities → Posts → Comments → Votes → Teardown**\n\n`Supabase: Sign-in` stores the JWT in `{{token}}`, which every authenticated request\ninherits as a Bearer token via the collection's auth setting. Each create step saves\nthe new record's id for the requests that follow.\n\nHeadless, via newman:\n\nnewman run superForum.postman_collection.json -e your-env.json\n\n\n\n## Notes\n\n- `Supabase: Sign-up` and `API: Create Profile` have lasting side effects (a Supabase\n  user and a profile row). They succeed on the first run and return \"already exists\"\n  on later runs — that's expected, and the collection stays green.\n- Teardown deletes the comment, post, and community it created, so a completed run\n  leaves the database as it found it.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "55891424"
  },
